WEBVTT

00:06.375 --> 00:08.916
Okay, people, we need to talk.

00:09.833 --> 00:11.875
And it's pretty serious.

00:13.833 --> 00:17.083
It's about our new tenant,
Tsukinomori Mashiro.

00:17.625 --> 00:20.999
I'd like to throw a welcome party
for her next Friday at 8 PM.

00:21.000 --> 00:25.707
Hm... Would she even come
if we invited her, though?

00:25.708 --> 00:26.999
I have a plan.

00:27.000 --> 00:29.458
I just need everyone's help to make it work.

00:29.791 --> 00:33.000
Let's show her how much of a pain we can be!

00:58.583 --> 01:04.250
MY FRIEND'S LITTLE SISTER HAS IT IN FOR ME!

02:04.416 --> 02:06.832
Let's turn back the clock a bit.

02:06.833 --> 02:09.916
In celebration of the update
with our new character and scenario!

02:10.291 --> 02:12.333
Cheers!

02:18.625 --> 02:21.958
Nothing beats a drink
after you've met a deadline!

02:22.333 --> 02:25.582
You really had me pulling
my hair out this time, you know.

02:25.583 --> 02:28.082
Sumire-chan-sensei, you reek of booze!

02:28.083 --> 02:29.707
How many have you had already?

02:29.708 --> 02:32.875
Aw, like I'm gonna keep track.

02:34.416 --> 02:35.749
Want anything to eat?

02:35.750 --> 02:37.375
Pass me those snacks.

02:37.666 --> 02:38.749
Sure.

02:38.750 --> 02:40.333
You're being awfully docile tonight.

02:41.416 --> 02:47.541
Well, you guys invited me here, even though
I'm not a member of 05th Floor Alliance.

02:48.333 --> 02:53.208
Seeing her like this makes me realize
just what a pain she normally is toward me.

02:53.750 --> 02:56.541
Wow, this roast beef's really good.

02:57.666 --> 02:59.500
You cooked it yourself, Aki?

03:00.000 --> 03:02.207
Yep. It was easier than you'd think.

03:02.208 --> 03:04.165
You really are a man of many talents.

03:04.166 --> 03:07.250
As always, I don't need to hear that from you.

03:08.083 --> 03:11.624
Just like with this update. No other
engineer could've made that deadline.

03:11.625 --> 03:12.791
'Preciate ya!

03:13.208 --> 03:15.040
It sure was down to the wire, huh?

03:15.041 --> 03:16.415
We would've been in trouble

03:16.416 --> 03:21.082
if I hadn't set up Sensei's computer
to upload her files automatically.

03:21.083 --> 03:25.665
What kind of program did you write
to pull off something that crazy?

03:25.666 --> 03:28.750
I just thought it'd come in handy.

03:29.166 --> 03:31.000
You say that like it's easy to do.

03:33.041 --> 03:35.250
He really is a genius.

03:35.708 --> 03:38.250
There's no one alive
who can hold a candle to you.

03:39.458 --> 03:41.415
Maybe not.

03:41.416 --> 03:45.500
But this skill is nothing but a disease
if you don't know how to apply it.

03:46.000 --> 03:49.582
I'm who I am now because you
put me on the right path.

03:49.583 --> 03:52.500
In my mind, that makes you
far more special than me.

03:53.583 --> 03:56.458
I'm not really into talking about the past.

03:58.958 --> 04:01.124
Where's Makigai-sensei, anyway?

04:01.125 --> 04:05.291
Couldn't make it this week
because of a deadline coming up.

04:05.583 --> 04:06.999
Makigai Namako.

04:07.000 --> 04:09.415
Winner of the grand prize
in the newcomer awards

04:09.416 --> 04:12.291
of the popular light novel imprint,
UZA Bunko, three years ago.

04:13.208 --> 04:16.124
The winning series sold
over three million copies,

04:16.125 --> 04:20.374
marking the explosive debut of Makigai Namako
as the hot new author to watch for—

04:20.375 --> 04:23.541
and as the scenario writer
of 05th Floor Alliance.

04:24.208 --> 04:28.040
I enclosed a commission along with a
fan letter, figuring I had nothing to lose...

04:28.041 --> 04:31.291
and by some miracle, I got a reply!

04:31.666 --> 04:32.832
We haven't met in person,

04:32.833 --> 04:36.457
but from our chats, they seem like
a friendly guy a bit older than me.

04:36.458 --> 04:37.999
That's unusual.

04:38.000 --> 04:41.624
Yeah, well, I'm sure working adults
have a lot to deal with.

04:41.625 --> 04:42.666
Like her.

04:42.791 --> 04:44.374
Say what?!

04:44.375 --> 04:47.040
You badmouthin' me or somethin'?

04:47.041 --> 04:50.124
No. We're talking about Makigai-sensei.

04:50.125 --> 04:51.665
Aw...

04:51.666 --> 04:53.665
You're sloshed already?!

04:53.666 --> 04:55.666
Iroha! What did you give her?

04:55.791 --> 04:59.332
Well, she started mixing her own at some point.

04:59.333 --> 05:00.332
Bring it on, damn it!

05:00.333 --> 05:01.374
She was using this.

05:01.375 --> 05:02.833
That's shochu!

05:03.166 --> 05:07.040
Oh, gosh! I'm startin' to feel really good!

05:07.041 --> 05:10.958
Akiteru-sama, come soothe my burning body!

05:11.416 --> 05:12.625
I swear...

05:13.375 --> 05:16.333
Okay, people, we need to talk.

05:18.166 --> 05:20.457
And it's pretty serious.

05:20.458 --> 05:22.416
SIX DAYS BEFORE THE WELCOME PARTY (SATURDAY)

05:37.000 --> 05:38.582
W-Would you pipe down?

05:38.583 --> 05:41.083
The weekend is for sleeping in!
What is wrong with you?

05:41.375 --> 05:45.333
I'm hosting a dinner party at my
place this Friday. Can you come?

05:48.791 --> 05:51.666
FIVE DAYS BEFORE THE WELCOME PARTY (SUNDAY)

05:52.041 --> 05:54.458
Hm? It's not ringing?

05:55.041 --> 05:57.333
Did she cut off the power?

05:58.166 --> 05:59.665
Maybe I should give up for today.

05:59.666 --> 06:02.166
Is that what you were hoping I'd say?

06:04.416 --> 06:06.916
DINNER PARTY INVITATION
6:00 PM FRIDAY AT APARTMENT 502

06:08.291 --> 06:09.249
Huh?

06:09.250 --> 06:11.833
FOUR DAYS BEFORE THE WELCOME PARTY (MONDAY)

06:19.833 --> 06:21.625
I NEED TO TALK TO YOU.

06:25.500 --> 06:28.207
WHAT WAS THAT YESTERDAY? BULLYING? HARASSMENT?

06:28.208 --> 06:30.290
AN INVITATION TO A DINNER PARTY, LIKE IT SAID.

06:30.291 --> 06:32.540
YOU TURNED MY MAILBOX
INTO A TRASH CAN FOR THAT?

06:32.541 --> 06:33.958
JUST GIVE ME YOUR LIME ID ALREADY.

06:35.000 --> 06:36.875
OVER MY DEAD BODY.

06:39.625 --> 06:42.665
That's okay. There's still time.

06:42.666 --> 06:45.665
Hey, Mashiro. Let me see your notebook.

06:45.666 --> 06:47.249
Say, about this Friday—

06:47.250 --> 06:48.875
Don't talk to me.

06:49.208 --> 06:51.708
TWO DAYS BEFORE THE WELCOME PARTY (WEDNESDAY)

06:53.916 --> 06:55.541
Hey! So about this Friday—

06:55.916 --> 06:58.957
Could you not lie in wait for me?
What are you, a stalker?

06:58.958 --> 07:00.082
Hey.

07:00.083 --> 07:01.708
About tomorrow...

07:02.500 --> 07:05.041
I want to throw a welcome party
for you at my place.

07:05.375 --> 07:09.249
If we're gonna be living on the same floor,
we might as well have fun, right?

07:09.250 --> 07:10.458
Look...

07:11.625 --> 07:14.375
This is not the place for
one of your smug looks.

07:17.000 --> 07:18.291
What to do...

07:21.208 --> 07:24.166
Let's see... What else do we need?

07:26.166 --> 07:27.332
Care for a sample?

07:27.333 --> 07:29.166
Those look tasty!

07:32.708 --> 07:36.624
It's so good! Something rich
is oozing out from inside...

07:36.625 --> 07:38.915
They're stuffed with cheese.

07:38.916 --> 07:40.708
Wanna try one, Senpai?

07:41.083 --> 07:43.208
Here! Open wide!

07:43.666 --> 07:47.082
- Stop, idiot.
- Aw, there's no need to be embarrassed.

07:47.083 --> 07:50.165
Really! How mean of him
to call you an idiot, missus!

07:50.166 --> 07:51.540
I know, right?

07:51.541 --> 07:52.915
She's not my missus!

07:52.916 --> 07:56.000
You're not going to eat it, Senpai?

07:56.291 --> 07:57.916
No, I'm not.

07:58.458 --> 08:00.708
I... see...

08:01.416 --> 08:04.041
Just eat it! For your girlfriend's sake!

08:04.666 --> 08:08.125
Oh, fine! I'll eat it, okay?!

08:09.291 --> 08:12.082
It's fine. Sorry for trying to force you.

08:12.083 --> 08:13.832
I didn't think you were forcing anything.

08:13.833 --> 08:14.958
Then...

08:15.333 --> 08:17.958
Beg me for it. And make it cute.

08:18.291 --> 08:20.165
This bitch!

08:20.166 --> 08:24.457
I... I really want to eat that.
From the bottom of my heart.

08:24.458 --> 08:26.332
You don't seem very serious.

08:26.333 --> 08:27.832
I want to eat it like crazy.

08:27.833 --> 08:30.500
Do you want me to feed it to you?

08:30.916 --> 08:33.166
Yes! I want you to feed it to me!

08:35.041 --> 08:37.041
I'll make you pay for this one day!

08:37.333 --> 08:38.707
You pass.

08:38.708 --> 08:40.416
Okay, here's your reward.

08:43.583 --> 08:46.165
- Do you like it, Senpai?
- Damn it!

08:46.166 --> 08:47.458
It's really good.

08:48.250 --> 08:51.833
- I love that honest side of you, Senpai!
- How cute.

08:53.791 --> 08:58.040
I don't know how you can
constantly lie about loving people.

08:58.041 --> 09:01.415
What? It's not like
I'd say that to just anyone.

09:01.416 --> 09:03.875
And I say it to you because it's true!

09:04.291 --> 09:06.458
She and you really are polar opposites.

09:06.583 --> 09:09.582
Let me guess...
You're talking about Mashiro-senpai?

09:09.583 --> 09:13.041
Yes. All she says whenever she
sees me is "I hate you" and "Die."

09:13.916 --> 09:18.124
Speaking of, you still haven't gotten her
to accept the invite, have you?

09:18.125 --> 09:21.624
Yeah, well, she's completely avoiding me now.

09:21.625 --> 09:23.083
I'm not sure what to do.

09:28.041 --> 09:31.666
Senpai, you're not holding back
on her account, are you?

09:32.166 --> 09:34.999
Compared to how you are
when you get serious,

09:35.000 --> 09:39.750
it feels like you've barely been trying.

09:41.791 --> 09:45.333
Most of the time, you're infuriatingly pushy.

09:46.666 --> 09:50.415
Like when you suggested my brother and
Sumire-chan-sensei join HPW with you.

09:50.416 --> 09:53.833
It seemed like the best option for us.
I couldn't help myself.

09:54.333 --> 09:56.624
And you managed to convince them.

09:56.625 --> 09:59.165
You must be a really good judge of people.

09:59.166 --> 10:02.457
It's like you somehow know
exactly what everyone wants.

10:02.458 --> 10:07.207
It bugs me to see people with talent
in a place where they're unable to use it.

10:07.208 --> 10:11.290
When someone can't use their
talents to do what they love,

10:11.291 --> 10:13.166
it's a total waste.

10:14.333 --> 10:17.832
Reaching out to those struggling with
the rift between their dreams and reality,

10:17.833 --> 10:20.832
and using your ability as producer
to help them close that gap...

10:20.833 --> 10:23.541
That's where you shine, right?

10:24.416 --> 10:25.458
Got it!

10:29.708 --> 10:31.708
Be more careful, idiot.

10:35.000 --> 10:36.708
You sure saved my skin!

10:37.375 --> 10:41.707
When I take advantage of my free rein
to do something dumb, you catch me.

10:41.708 --> 10:44.666
That's why my brother sticks with you, too.

10:45.250 --> 10:47.415
If you ever lose faith
and don't know what to do,

10:47.416 --> 10:50.750
just believe in yourself,
and it'll be okay! I guarantee it!

10:52.375 --> 10:53.957
Thanks, Iroha.

10:53.958 --> 10:55.833
You're right.

10:56.458 --> 10:58.457
You'd better be ready, Mashiro.

10:58.458 --> 11:00.832
I've really got it in for you now.

11:00.833 --> 11:02.165
DINNER PARTY INVITATION
6:00 PM FRIDAY AT APARTMENT 502

11:02.166 --> 11:03.666
Tomorrow...

11:05.750 --> 11:06.875
I'm not going.

11:07.500 --> 11:11.833
Even if Aki invites me,
there's no way I'm going.

11:12.333 --> 11:15.333
MY FRIEND'S LITTLE SISTER HAS IT IN FOR ME!

11:23.375 --> 11:25.040
Well, that's fine.

11:25.041 --> 11:26.333
Everything ready?

11:26.958 --> 11:28.583
Yep, all ready.

11:28.916 --> 11:32.249
I can't believe you made me put
this whole thing together in a week.

11:32.250 --> 11:34.582
I'll pay you back one day, I promise.

11:34.583 --> 11:35.749
I'll hold you to it.

11:35.750 --> 11:37.665
AKI, OZ, MURASAKI SHIKIBU-SENSEI, IROHA

11:37.666 --> 11:39.874
Operation PT is underway!

11:39.875 --> 11:41.500
Places, people!

11:41.791 --> 11:42.833
Roger!

11:45.750 --> 11:46.791
Mashiro!

11:48.041 --> 11:50.624
Wh-What? Why'd you come running after me?

11:50.625 --> 11:53.457
I-I told you I'm not going
to your dinner party.

11:53.458 --> 11:56.791
But you remembered it. That means your
interest level is above zero, at least.

11:57.416 --> 11:58.624
D-Don't give me that!

11:58.625 --> 12:02.290
With you bugging me every single day,
I couldn't forget, even if I wanted to!

12:02.291 --> 12:05.457
Yeah, maybe. But don't worry.

12:05.458 --> 12:08.290
I won't drag you there
against your will or anything.

12:08.291 --> 12:09.457
Really?

12:09.458 --> 12:11.582
Yeah. I don't lie.

12:11.583 --> 12:13.166
I can practically see the script.

12:13.500 --> 12:15.665
That's not why I chased you down, though.

12:15.666 --> 12:17.875
I just thought we could walk home together.

12:19.125 --> 12:21.208
We're going in the same direction, anyway.

12:21.333 --> 12:23.250
It won't hurt if I'm with you, right?

12:24.041 --> 12:26.791
Surely she won't have a problem with—

12:28.791 --> 12:31.791
Seriously? She hates me that much?

12:32.166 --> 12:35.540
You won't escape! We're walking
home together, whatever it takes!

12:35.541 --> 12:37.333
Mashiro!

12:50.416 --> 12:53.000
Wh-Why are you chasing me?!

12:53.250 --> 12:55.082
Don't think so highly of yourself!

12:55.083 --> 12:57.916
I'm just heading back
to my own place! That's all!

12:59.333 --> 13:02.708
Then it shouldn't be necessary
to run at full speed!

13:03.208 --> 13:04.457
Hey, wait!

13:04.458 --> 13:06.166
You're going home, right?

13:06.291 --> 13:08.250
Then stop chasing me!

13:10.250 --> 13:12.290
Shut up! What's wrong with me chasing you?!

13:12.291 --> 13:13.750
Now you're getting angry?!

13:22.208 --> 13:23.915
Why concern yourself with me?

13:23.916 --> 13:26.708
You'd enjoy your life just fine without me!

13:28.875 --> 13:32.333
I can't just join a community
that's already been established.

13:34.333 --> 13:38.083
Okay, but if you're not gonna join
our circle, where are you going?

13:39.416 --> 13:42.082
Who have you spoken to
this past week, other than me?

13:42.083 --> 13:44.290
How many classmates
have you conversed with?

13:44.291 --> 13:46.083
Stop it. Don't ask me that.

13:46.750 --> 13:49.125
Apparently, she was being bullied.

13:49.250 --> 13:53.665
Is this the kind of life that you
transferred schools to obtain?

13:53.666 --> 13:54.958
It can't be!

13:57.958 --> 14:00.999
What happened at the restaurant
was my fault. I admit that.

14:01.000 --> 14:03.082
I'll apologize for it
as many times as you want.

14:03.083 --> 14:04.832
But I won't ask you to forgive me.

14:04.833 --> 14:07.707
If you want to keep hating me, that's fine.

14:07.708 --> 14:08.999
But...

14:09.000 --> 14:12.291
Don't lie to yourself
and pretend everything's okay!

14:15.916 --> 14:17.000
Mashiro?

14:18.041 --> 14:19.416
Stop... it...

14:29.375 --> 14:31.041
You okay, Mashiro—

14:32.916 --> 14:34.375
Damn, that's sexy!

14:37.541 --> 14:39.540
Wh-What are you looking at, you pervert?!

14:39.541 --> 14:41.915
S-Sorry! You looked so sexy,
I just couldn't help it!

14:41.916 --> 14:43.041
I don't need to hear that!

14:53.166 --> 14:55.791
Tell me when you're able to stand on your own.

14:57.583 --> 14:59.291
O-Okay.

15:04.333 --> 15:06.290
Today really sucked.

15:06.291 --> 15:08.665
Excuse me, that's my line!

15:08.666 --> 15:10.666
You still won't admit it?

15:11.208 --> 15:14.875
We've even got a matching "drowned rat" look
going. Anyone would think we were a couple.

15:18.750 --> 15:20.500
What the heck? Are you crazy?

15:20.833 --> 15:24.041
This is the worst matching look I've ever seen.

15:24.875 --> 15:28.457
Maybe it's the gods' way of
blessing our fake relationship.

15:28.458 --> 15:30.540
Any god who'd do that should just die.

15:30.541 --> 15:32.874
Wow, that's pretty harsh.

15:32.875 --> 15:36.749
If you start praying, they might give you
a reason to feel good someday, too.

15:36.750 --> 15:38.749
I'm not getting my hopes up.

15:38.750 --> 15:42.333
People who hated me up until yesterday
aren't gonna start liking me tomorrow.

15:42.708 --> 15:45.374
That might be true, but...

15:45.375 --> 15:47.624
Why are you so stubborn, anyway?

15:47.625 --> 15:49.499
You're just weird.

15:49.500 --> 15:54.708
Why concern yourself with me so much
just because my dad asked you to?

15:55.750 --> 15:58.332
Wait, no. None of this is your fault.

15:58.333 --> 16:00.208
I don't hate you.

16:00.666 --> 16:04.290
So... please don't hate me.

16:04.291 --> 16:06.749
No one ever said they hated you.

16:06.750 --> 16:09.000
They think you hate them, though.

16:09.416 --> 16:12.375
The thing is... I'm scared.

16:12.958 --> 16:16.374
What if I don't fit in
with your circle of friends?

16:16.375 --> 16:19.874
What if I just blend into the background,
and nobody even looks at me?

16:19.875 --> 16:25.208
I feel like, from that moment,
you won't see me anymore, either.

16:25.750 --> 16:29.082
I know it's weird. It makes no sense, but...

16:29.083 --> 16:30.749
No, it's not weird.

16:30.750 --> 16:31.875
Huh?

16:32.125 --> 16:37.165
It might not seem like it since the whole
fake couple thing drew attention to us,

16:37.166 --> 16:40.583
but I was always just part of
the background in class anyway.

16:41.166 --> 16:42.499
N-No way...

16:42.500 --> 16:44.457
I don't have any particular skills,

16:44.458 --> 16:47.082
and it's not like I'm an academic prodigy.

16:47.083 --> 16:49.040
I'm not that good-looking, either.

16:49.041 --> 16:52.207
I'm an average guy who's average
at everything. In other words, boring.

16:52.208 --> 16:53.374
That's who I am.

16:53.375 --> 16:57.124
That's not true! You're the leader
of 05th Floor Alliance, and...

16:57.125 --> 16:59.332
Huh? You know about that?

16:59.333 --> 17:02.208
Um, well, my dad mentioned it.

17:02.583 --> 17:04.832
You created a really amazing game, right?

17:04.833 --> 17:07.290
Dad said you've made a ton of money.

17:07.291 --> 17:10.749
Most of it goes right back into
developing the game, though.

17:10.750 --> 17:15.374
I think that's amazing. You could
be the most popular kid in class.

17:15.375 --> 17:17.166
I keep it secret at school.

17:17.958 --> 17:20.999
Why? Because you think people
might make fun of you?

17:21.000 --> 17:22.166
That's not it.

17:22.625 --> 17:26.625
I could too easily imagine myself
getting a big head from all the attention.

17:28.000 --> 17:30.249
You don't want everyone to praise you?

17:30.250 --> 17:32.665
I mean, sure, I want that.

17:32.666 --> 17:36.666
But when I think of all the time
I'd waste if I bragged about it,

17:37.000 --> 17:40.125
it seems more efficient to just
keep it hidden from everyone.

17:44.625 --> 17:45.833
Aki, you really are...

17:46.291 --> 17:47.750
way too weird.

17:49.500 --> 17:50.707
You really won't be coming?

17:50.708 --> 17:54.165
Sorry. I'm happy you invited me, but...

17:54.166 --> 17:55.874
They're all good people.

17:55.875 --> 17:58.332
They won't exclude you from the group.
I can promise you that.

17:58.333 --> 18:01.457
I know. It's just a matter of how I feel.

18:01.458 --> 18:03.957
Well, nothing you can do about that, I guess.

18:03.958 --> 18:05.750
Okay. Later, then.

18:08.458 --> 18:11.458
Can you please treat me
normally starting next week?

18:12.625 --> 18:13.666
Okay.

18:15.416 --> 18:16.500
Huh?

18:17.875 --> 18:19.041
The door's open...

18:19.500 --> 18:20.624
Did someone break in?!

18:20.625 --> 18:21.833
I don't know.

18:21.958 --> 18:25.291
- Let's check. I'll go in with you.
- Okay.

18:36.833 --> 18:39.833
If you can't get your feelings
on board, I'll give up.

18:39.958 --> 18:42.541
- I'll respect your wishes.
- Huh?

18:46.833 --> 18:48.458
But it's not gonna turn out that way...

18:49.125 --> 18:50.750
if I have any say in it!

18:51.666 --> 18:54.250
Welcome to the fifth floor!

18:57.208 --> 18:58.999
Wh-What is this?

18:59.000 --> 19:00.999
It's your welcome party.

19:01.000 --> 19:02.624
That's not what I mean.

19:02.625 --> 19:05.333
Why did you let yourselves into my apartment?

19:06.125 --> 19:08.415
Sorry, but this is actually my apartment.

19:08.416 --> 19:12.874
What? But the one at the end
is supposed to be mine...

19:12.875 --> 19:15.125
This isn't the one at the end, though.

19:15.583 --> 19:18.665
We just put up a screen
to make it look like the end.

19:18.666 --> 19:22.415
We worked pretty hard making it
look exactly like the wall!

19:22.416 --> 19:23.540
- Right?
- Yep.

19:23.541 --> 19:27.207
Operation PT—short for "picture trick"—

19:27.208 --> 19:28.375
worked like a charm!

19:30.291 --> 19:32.000
I don't get it.

19:32.291 --> 19:35.708
Why go this far?
Do you really want so badly to...

19:36.333 --> 19:37.416
Yeah.

19:38.500 --> 19:42.125
You'll understand them
once you join the group.

19:44.625 --> 19:46.957
B-But... we can't just be friends right away—

19:46.958 --> 19:51.540
Oh, no worries there! The four of us here
aren't even "friends," exactly.

19:51.541 --> 19:52.582
Huh?

19:52.583 --> 19:56.165
Or at least, not outside of
Senpai and my brother.

19:56.166 --> 20:00.915
In fact, as a little sister, it'd be a lot more
interesting for me if they were a couple.

20:00.916 --> 20:02.875
I get it! That'd be a such a hit!

20:03.250 --> 20:06.374
The calm, sadistic, perfect top,
and the princely bottom!

20:06.375 --> 20:08.750
They'd have the perfect harmony!

20:08.875 --> 20:11.040
Have you been drinking already?

20:11.041 --> 20:12.625
Not that pressure point!

20:13.000 --> 20:15.415
We all just happen to live on the same floor,

20:15.416 --> 20:19.374
so we figured we might as well do
other stuff together, too. That's all.

20:19.375 --> 20:22.249
Because you all work on the game together?

20:22.250 --> 20:24.415
Oh, you know about that?

20:24.416 --> 20:28.707
- I feel so much better!
- I'm not involved with it at all, though.

20:28.708 --> 20:30.915
That's... true...

20:30.916 --> 20:33.207
Anyway, that's how it is.

20:33.208 --> 20:38.207
You can just consider these guys
your fake boyfriend's friends

20:38.208 --> 20:40.625
and your fake boyfriend's
friend's little sister.

20:41.458 --> 20:44.415
There's no obligation to be
part of 05th Floor Alliance,

20:44.416 --> 20:47.041
and no bothersome ties chaining us together.

20:48.666 --> 20:52.665
I've never met Makigai Namako-sensei in person,

20:52.666 --> 20:55.750
but that hasn't changed our relationship.

20:58.416 --> 21:00.375
Do you understand now?

21:02.125 --> 21:05.791
Tricking me into this surprise
was low. Seriously.

21:06.166 --> 21:08.458
Yeah, but this isn't so bad, right?

21:10.833 --> 21:11.916
Yeah.

21:13.208 --> 21:14.458
Thank you!

21:16.291 --> 21:18.207
Well, shall we get started?

21:18.208 --> 21:19.624
I'm gonna drink!

21:19.625 --> 21:22.125
You already have been, though.

21:24.333 --> 21:28.208
Translation: Becky Cottrill

21:28.583 --> 21:31.666
Subtitle Editing: Geoff Mazzolini
Subtitle Timing: Krzysztof Kunc

21:32.208 --> 21:35.541
Quality Control: Gabriella Ramirez
Translation Check: David Saylor

23:05.500 --> 23:06.707
What do you want?

23:06.708 --> 23:09.415
Good job with all that
Mashiro-senpai business.

23:09.416 --> 23:12.415
- Thanks.
- You really are such a nice person.

23:12.416 --> 23:13.915
Where's this coming from?

23:13.916 --> 23:14.957
I mean...

23:14.958 --> 23:18.791
I do the voice acting for
05th Floor Alliance's game,

23:19.666 --> 23:24.166
but you let me be part of the group
without telling anyone about it.

23:24.791 --> 23:29.750
DON'T MISS THE NEXT EPISODE...
